---
import Galaxy from '../../components/Galaxy.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import BookCover from '../../components/BookCover.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { site, book } from '../../data/site';
import { differences, read, parts, appendices, faqs, arc, rhythm } from '../../data/book';
import { img, media } from '../../lib/media';

const bookLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Book',
  name: book.title,
  alternativeHeadline: book.subtitle,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Nimrod Dvir' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: site.name, url: site.url },
  bookFormat: 'https://schema.org/EBook',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  url: `${site.url}/books/${book.slug}/`,
  image: img(media.cover, 800),
  numberOfPages: undefined,
  educationalLevel: 'Undergraduate',
  about: ['Databases', 'SQL', 'Management information systems', 'Business intelligence'],
};
---

<Base
  title={book.title}
  description="An interactive, business-first database textbook. Students write real SQL from the first weeks, build two complete systems, and learn to turn data into decisions they can defend."
  headerTone="night"
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(bookLd)} />

  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="book-hero on-night">
    <Galaxy />
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow reveal">Interactive textbook · {book.chapters} chapters</p>
        <h1 class="reveal" style="--d:.06s">{book.title}</h1>
        <p class="subtitle reveal" style="--d:.1s">{book.subtitle}</p>
        <p class="author reveal" style="--d:.12s">by {book.author}</p>
        <p class="lede reveal" style="--d:.16s">
          A database course for people who will make decisions with data, not just store it. Students write real SQL
          from the first weeks, build two complete systems, and finish able to turn a pile of rows into a
          recommendation they can stand behind.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row reveal" style="--d:.2s">
          <a class="btn gold" href={book.readerUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start reading <Icon name="external" size={16} /></a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/contact/?topic=instructor">Request a review copy</a>
        </div>
        <dl class="meta reveal" style="--d:.26s">
          <div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Interactive web book</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Works on</dt><dd>Laptop, tablet, phone</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Level</dt><dd>Undergraduate, no coding needed</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Access</dt><dd>{book.price ? book.price : 'Course & individual pricing on request'}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="cover-wrap reveal" style="--d:.1s">
        <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <BookCover width={400} eager />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HUMAN DESCRIPTION ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story">
      <aside class="reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
        <p class="pull">“I understand the terms, but not how they connect.”</p>
        <p class="pull-cite">What students kept saying. This book is the answer.</p>
        <p class="aside-lede">
          The hard part of a database course isn’t the syntax. It’s knowing which question is worth asking, and
          trusting the answer enough to act on it. This book is written for students who will run teams, budgets and
          companies, and it teaches data the way they’ll use it: starting with a real decision, and ending with a
          recommendation they can defend.
        </p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose-lg reveal" style="--d:.08s">
        <p class="dropcap">
          Here is what nobody says out loud in a database class: the syntax is the easy part. The hard part is knowing
          which question is worth asking, getting the right data to answer it, and trusting the answer enough to put
          your name on a recommendation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <em>Using Data to Drive Business Performance</em> is built around that hard part. It starts where business
          starts, with a decision somebody needs to make. Within the first few weeks you are writing SQL against a
          real database, right in your browser, to answer questions a manager would actually ask. Once you have felt
          what good data makes possible, the book turns around and teaches you how to design it well: tables,
          relationships, normalization, security, the whole foundation.
        </p>
        <p>
          It reads like a good teacher talking, not a reference manual. Every chapter follows the same rhythm, so you
          always know where you are. And it doesn’t stop at the query. You build reports, read KPIs honestly, and write
          the short memo that turns evidence into action, because that is the part your future boss will care about.
        </p>
        <p>
          It was written and rewritten in a real classroom, semester after semester, with real students telling us
          exactly where they got lost. Those spots are now the clearest pages in the book.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ DIFFERENCES ============ -->
  <section class="section on-paper-2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this book is different</p>
        <h2>A database course that finally feels like <em class="gold">business</em>.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Students tell us the same things: “I know the terms but not how they connect.” “We learn SQL, but I
          don’t know why it matters.” So we built the book around those two sentences.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        {
          differences.map((d, i) => (
            <article class="card diff reveal" style={`--d:${(i % 3) * 0.08}s`}>
              <span class="ico"><Icon name={d.icon} size={24} /></span>
              <h3>{d.title}</h3>
              <p>{d.body}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ LEARNING ARC ============ -->
  <section class="section tight on-paper-2 arc-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The learning arc</p>
        <h2>From a single number to a confident decision.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="arc reveal">
        {
          arc.map((step, i) => (
            <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
              <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span class="step">{step}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ R.E.A.D. ============ -->
  <section class="section on-night">
    <Galaxy />
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">A habit, not a formula</p>
        <h2>R.E.A.D. — the four moves behind every good data decision.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="read-grid">
        {
          read.map((r, i) => (
            <div class="read reveal" style={`--d:${i * 0.08}s`}>
              <span class="letter">{r.letter}</span>
              <h3>{r.word}</h3>
              <p>{r.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ RHYTHM ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split rhythm-split">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Inside every chapter</p>
        <h2>The same steady rhythm, so you always know where you are.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Every chapter moves through six parts, from the big idea to work you can show someone. Instructors get a
          predictable structure that maps cleanly onto any LMS; students get a path that never leaves them
          guessing.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="#contents">See the full table of contents →</a>
      </div>
      <ol class="rhythm">
        {
          rhythm.map((r, i) => (
            <li class="reveal" style={`--d:${i * 0.06}s`}>
              <span class="n">{r.n}</span>
              <div>
                <h4>{r.title}</h4>
                <p>{r.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PROJECTS ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Two running projects</p>
        <h2>Watch real systems grow, one chapter at a time.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <article class="card project reveal">
          <span class="tag">Guided</span>
          <h3>The Grading Database</h3>
          <p>
            Every student already understands grades, which makes it the perfect first system. You query it, find its
            flaws, normalize it, secure it and report on it, chapter by chapter, with the book walking beside you.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><Icon name="check" size={18} /> Familiar data, real complexity</li>
            <li><Icon name="check" size={18} /> Powers every “Let’s Build” section</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card project reveal" style="--d:.08s">
          <span class="tag gold-tag">On your own</span>
          <h3>PetVax</h3>
          <p>
            A veterinary clinic with messy notes, appointments and vaccine records. Here you transfer what you learned
            to a system you have never seen, turning vague requirements into a working, defensible design.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><Icon name="check" size={18} /> Unseen scenario, independent work</li>
            <li><Icon name="check" size={18} /> Portfolio-ready by the end of term</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CONTENTS ============ -->
  <section class="section on-paper-2" id="contents">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Table of contents</p>
        <h2>Sixteen chapters, four movements.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="toc">
        {
          parts.map((p, i) => (
            <div class="part reveal" style={`--d:${(i % 2) * 0.08}s`}>
              <p class="part-label">{p.part}</p>
              <h3>{p.title}</h3>
              <ol>
                {p.chapters.map((c) => (
                  <li>
                    <span class="cn">{String(c.n).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                    <span>
                      <strong>{c.title}</strong>
                      <em>{c.note}</em>
                    </span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ol>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="appendices reveal">
        <h3>Appendices</h3>
        <ul>
          {
            appendices.map((a) => (
              <li>
                <strong>{a.title}</strong>
                <span>{a.note}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHO ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it’s for</p>
        <h2>Made for the people in the room.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        <article class="card who reveal">
          <Icon name="graduation" size={28} />
          <h3>Students</h3>
          <p>Business majors who never planned to write code, and are about to discover they can. Clear, friendly and honest about what matters.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card who reveal" style="--d:.08s">
          <Icon name="users" size={28} />
          <h3>Instructors</h3>
          <p>A predictable six-part chapter package, transfer labs, reading checks and artifacts students must explain. Less stitching, more teaching.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card who reveal" style="--d:.16s">
          <Icon name="building" size={28} />
          <h3>Programs</h3>
          <p>One integrated course instead of a theory text plus a separate software manual. Flexible enough for MIS, AIS, analytics and applied SQL.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CTA ============ -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-band on-night reveal">
        <Galaxy center={0.35} />
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">For instructors &amp; programs</p>
          <h2>Teaching this course next term?</h2>
          <p>Request a review copy, ask about course adoption, or tell us what your students need. A person reads every message.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <a class="btn gold" href="/contact/?topic=instructor">Request a review copy</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/contact/?topic=adoption">Talk about adoption</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- ============ ACCESS ============ -->
  <section class="section tight on-paper-2" id="access">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting access</p>
        <h2>Three ways in.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        <article class="card access reveal">
          <h3>Read online</h3>
          <p class="price">{book.price ?? 'Through your course'}</p>
          <p>Open the interactive reader and sign in with the access your course or instructor provides.</p>
          <a class="btn small" href={book.readerUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the reader <Icon name="external" size={14} /></a>
        </article>
        <article class="card access featured-access reveal" style="--d:.08s">
          <h3>Instructor review</h3>
          <p class="price">Complimentary</p>
          <p>Full access to the reader, chapter structure, labs and assessment materials for faculty evaluating the book.</p>
          <a class="btn gold small" href="/contact/?topic=instructor">Request review access</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card access reveal" style="--d:.16s">
          <h3>Course &amp; campus</h3>
          <p class="price">Custom pricing</p>
          <p>Section, department and institution-wide access, with LMS-friendly structure and onboarding support.</p>
          <a class="btn small" href="/contact/?topic=bulk">Ask about adoption</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="fine reveal">Purchases are covered by our <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a> and <a href="/terms/">terms</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2>Good questions, straight answers.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        {
          faqs.map((f) => (
            <details class="reveal">
              <summary>
                {f.q}
                <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
              </summary>
              <p>{f.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="end-cta on-night reveal">
        <Galaxy center={0.35} />
        <h2>Open it. Run a query. See for yourself.</h2>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn gold" href={book.readerUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start reading <Icon name="external" size={16} /></a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/contact/?topic=adoption">Talk to us about your course</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .book-hero {
    padding: clamp(48px, 7vw, 100px) 0 clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px);
    margin-top: calc(var(--header-h) * -1);
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + clamp(40px, 6vw, 88px));
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .book-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5.4vw, 4.6rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.2em;
  }
  .subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    color: #f0e6cf !important;
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }
  .author {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-bright) !important;
    margin-bottom: 1.8em;
  }
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .meta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px 28px;
    margin: 44px 0 0;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(233, 228, 216, 0.12);
  }
  .meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: #f6f1e4;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .cover-wrap {
    position: relative;
  }
  .glow {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 5% 10%;
    background: radial-gradient(closest-side, rgba(220, 182, 94, 0.5), transparent);
    filter: blur(40px);
  }

  .story {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 96px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .story aside {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + 32px);
  }
  .pull {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.6em;
  }
  .aside-lede {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .pull-cite {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .prose-lg p {
    font-size: clamp(1.06rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .dropcap::first-letter {
    float: left;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 4.6em;
    line-height: 0.82;
    padding: 0.06em 0.12em 0 0;
    color: var(--gold-deep);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .story {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .story aside {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  .ico {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--gold-wash);
    color: var(--gold-deep);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .diff p,
  .who p,
  .project p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }


  .read-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .read {
    padding: 28px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(233, 228, 216, 0.1);
  }
  .letter {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 4.2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #f1d58a, #b8892f);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .read p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .read-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .read-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 5px 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .gold-tag {
    background: var(--gold-wash);
    color: var(--gold-deep);
  }
  .ticks {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .ticks li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .ticks :global(svg) {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .toc {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .part {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px);
  }
  .part-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-deep);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .part ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
  }
  .part li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .cn {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .part strong {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .part em {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .appendices {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px);
    border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .appendices ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .appendices strong {
    display: block;
  }
  .appendices span {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .toc {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .who :global(svg) {
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .access {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .access p:not(.price) {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    flex: 1;
  }
  .access .btn {
    align-self: flex-start;
  }
  .price {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--gold-deep);
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }
  .featured-access {
    border-color: var(--gold);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--gold), var(--shadow);
  }
  .fine {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .fine a {
    color: var(--gold-deep);
  }

  .faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .faq summary {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 22px 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .plus {
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
  }
  .plus::before,
  .plus::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 0;
    width: 18px;
    height: 1.6px;
    background: var(--gold-deep);
    transition: transform 0.3s var(--ease);
  }
  .plus::after {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }
  details[open] .plus::after {
    transform: rotate(0);
  }
  .faq details p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
